#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b945e27-0b7f-548a-8c5f-a78ab5a43af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714301} {:answer/id #uuid "a4225577-9e92-58ef-966e-17ba5841a349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714312} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c38919-9225-5b78-a706-094e687a3415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714316} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d1208f-4f09-5dcb-b4af-f625b9cf2b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714318} {:answer/id #uuid "f465f656-377f-513e-bb88-901414285f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f465f656-377f-513e-bb88-901414285f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714324} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b0a1af-3821-55fd-a6ff-c6153a4b84ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6d90736c-cf2f-5782-be3b-fafcaba17ded" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-\\frac{3}{2}y &=3 \\\\ 1x+\\frac{1}{2}y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce its augmented matrix to row echelon form, with leading entry $1$ in every nonzero row. Select the pair giving **both** such a matrix and the complete general solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{y}{2} &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-1$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-1,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution.\n\nNormalize the remaining nonzero row using $R_2\\leftarrow -1R_2$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBoth nonzero rows now have leading entry $1$. The equation $0=1$ confirms that there is no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c317c66-0e60-5c3f-992a-55bf7355f1ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714295} {:answer/id #uuid "53f50d01-e04d-5cb3-a93e-a0c14deb9657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714303} {:answer/id #uuid "90bdf91b-e374-5a1c-b91e-c2785a32642e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714307} {:answer/id #uuid "9280bb8a-f4d3-5e5e-9916-9445e37fcecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714308} {:answer/id #uuid "e81b8d0e-a467-5e7e-b640-ce3fd1ce5cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e81b8d0e-a467-5e7e-b640-ce3fd1ce5cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714321} :answer-field/id #uuid "99abcc6c-9b20-50ff-8a39-c01f9a6aa145" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "93661add-a642-5623-8cc4-c24583525d9b" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+3y &=6 \\\\ 2x-2y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce its augmented matrix to row echelon form, with leading entry $1$ in every nonzero row. Select the pair giving **both** such a matrix and the complete general solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-1$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-1,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution.\n\nNormalize the remaining nonzero row using $R_2\\leftarrow -1R_2$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBoth nonzero rows now have leading entry $1$. The equation $0=1$ confirms that there is no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35c5cff7-c546-5690-906c-0d2f51c611f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714298} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba191eb-5e39-55a1-a07d-88150013a0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714304} {:answer/id #uuid "a74b5dd4-ffda-596e-a39b-de4a38da8f05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714313} {:answer/id #uuid "ea09bf1e-079a-5d32-aaf1-f0b87fe1ef3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714322} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9f0db6-df1e-5f5c-a6dd-0d92a68837fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea09bf1e-079a-5d32-aaf1-f0b87fe1ef3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714322} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab46842-665a-5b01-8533-b3bc83a37a13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c0d70e0e-0b84-55b7-a904-1dbf2c2fddd3" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y &=-4 \\\\ -3x+\\frac{9}{2}y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce its augmented matrix to row echelon form, with leading entry $1$ in every nonzero row. Select the pair giving **both** such a matrix and the complete general solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & \\frac{9}{2} & -7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & \\frac{9}{2} & -7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 2 \\\\ -3 & \\frac{9}{2} & -7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{3y}{2} &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-1$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-1,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution.\n\nNormalize the remaining nonzero row using $R_2\\leftarrow -1R_2$:\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBoth nonzero rows now have leading entry $1$. The equation $0=1$ confirms that there is no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25fb0c16-8e97-5dc4-b380-9663ed5e8a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714293} {:answer/id #uuid "347896ab-a7a9-5d4c-a8fb-df6e1b98e2e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714297} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3374de-4f53-5d63-bec3-16c7d55c9148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714300} {:answer/id #uuid "748e62bb-4f64-5ed4-9072-5bd6667d2709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714306} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c1672e-7cd4-5dab-85e4-2ae919b2da74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{6} & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a3374de-4f53-5d63-bec3-16c7d55c9148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714300} :answer-field/id #uuid "36405245-8025-51c1-94c8-bc78f6208cf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714299}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f4760a56-8b89-5907-965d-7cfbe5d54287" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-\\frac{3}{2}y &=9 \\\\ 3x+\\frac{3}{2}y &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce its augmented matrix to row echelon form, with leading entry $1$ in every nonzero row. Select the pair giving **both** such a matrix and the complete general solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 9 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{3}{2} & -9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 9 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{3}{2} & -9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{3}{2} & -9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{y}{2} &=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{y}{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-\\frac{y}{2}-3,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-\\frac{y}{2}-3 \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{y}{2}-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe zero row is redundant; the only nonzero row has leading entry $1$. Separating the constant and free-variable parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15204dd1-bd6a-5dfd-8656-dfdd2c4d1306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714292} {:answer/id #uuid "33179893-8435-56f7-a336-6daebf11bfea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714296} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d2d9cc-ed82-5910-b8ed-ed219a9a7d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714311} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ab0380-16ab-5173-b049-21e59415a5a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714314} {:answer/id #uuid "b606f41f-8585-5fb5-8f55-685aaac1af83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$; No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15204dd1-bd6a-5dfd-8656-dfdd2c4d1306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$; $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714292} :answer-field/id #uuid "5320f690-c605-588e-8b41-d939759095e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f83943bf-96d3-5825-8a7e-f7d8a6f48b5d" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-3y &=12 \\\\ -2x+2y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse Gaussian elimination to reduce its augmented matrix to row echelon form, with leading entry $1$ in every nonzero row. Select the pair giving **both** such a matrix and the complete general solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -3 & 12 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -3 & 12 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=4 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=y+4,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=y+4 \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}y+4 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe zero row is redundant; the only nonzero row has leading entry $1$. Separating the constant and free-variable parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad y\\in\\mathbb{R}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f578379-e268-5986-8867-dd50ef56da58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714416} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2bda9a-6825-5738-b85d-81bc320f2e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714421} {:answer/id #uuid "b5de2196-105e-5d8b-a38e-df6e5081983b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714434} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7894e4-f45a-53aa-954f-dd81cac48b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714435} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ca85de-240e-5b78-a62f-e811c0050933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f578379-e268-5986-8867-dd50ef56da58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714416} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c6cf8de-9051-59b6-8405-5abdcc501158" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "09e2c4a8-6e4e-5851-a812-a9d34e28f270" :question/problem "The vectors are given below.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nDetermine whether $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is a basis of $U=\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}$. If it is, find $x_1x_2$, where $\\mathbf{a}_3=x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2$. Otherwise, select the statement that it is not a basis." :question/worked-solution "A basis must be linearly independent and span $U$. The decomposition gives the system\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} &=-1 \\\\ -2x_{2} &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nIts augmented matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_{2}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThe reduced matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThere is a pivot in each of the $2$ coefficient columns, so the proposed vectors are linearly independent. The system is consistent, so the last vector is in their span. Their span therefore equals $U$, and $\\mathcal{B}$ is a basis.\n\nThe coefficients are $x_{1}=-1$, $x_{2}=2$.\nThus\n$$\nx_1x_2=\\left(-1\\right)\\left(2\\right)=-2.\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09be76b7-5ab6-52ca-a65b-5d8b17bc66cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714409} {:answer/id #uuid "40810fe2-a531-5d90-8e79-258281788f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714414} {:answer/id #uuid "83e150a2-7b9c-5f1a-9f1c-675408a9aa15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714426} {:answer/id #uuid "979f89e9-2929-5668-80e8-54d2cbb5fd31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714430} {:answer/id #uuid "b16bc3f5-c428-5a7a-a2e2-6cf805c0c610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83e150a2-7b9c-5f1a-9f1c-675408a9aa15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714426} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc4f4cb-899e-5a1e-bb43-7fc65748826e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6e2025d1-d37b-5319-91ef-c5d302066c0e" :question/problem "The vectors are given below.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nDetermine whether $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is a basis of $U=\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}$. If it is, find $x_1x_2$, where $\\mathbf{a}_3=x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2$. Otherwise, select the statement that it is not a basis." :question/worked-solution "A basis must be linearly independent and span $U$. The decomposition gives the system\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x_{1}+x_{2} &=-4 \\\\ 4x_{1}+2x_{2} &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nIts augmented matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{1}\\leftarrow \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow R_{2}-4R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow \\left(-1\\right)R_{2}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{1}\\leftarrow R_{1}+2R_{2}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThe reduced matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nOnly $1$ coefficient columns contain pivots. Thus the proposed vectors are linearly dependent. The augmented column contains a pivot; a reduced row says $0=1$. The last vector is outside the proposed span, so spanning also fails. Therefore, $\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$; the conditional coefficient calculation does not apply."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b0fa691-6f2c-5839-a730-21a7cadbdd26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714413} {:answer/id #uuid "55aea515-ae60-5ed1-9ba1-9d50514913c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714418} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2d41a5-0781-56b7-8b27-bb5760391a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714419} {:answer/id #uuid "87fd779e-dbb5-55a2-8938-1bf471beddd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714427} {:answer/id #uuid "c9101d45-13c4-5660-b245-61cf4333ed56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9101d45-13c4-5660-b245-61cf4333ed56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714439} :answer-field/id #uuid "766eee26-38df-5c7d-927a-30186e842b2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "95b56847-8bac-5366-820d-e8f76db82250" :question/problem "The vectors are given below.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nDetermine whether $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is a basis of $U=\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}$. If it is, find $x_1x_2$, where $\\mathbf{a}_3=x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2$. Otherwise, select the statement that it is not a basis." :question/worked-solution "A basis must be linearly independent and span $U$. The decomposition gives the system\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1}-2x_{2} &=0 \\\\ -x_{1}-x_{2} &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nIts augmented matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow R_{2}+R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)R_{2}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{1}\\leftarrow R_{1}+2R_{2}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThe reduced matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThere is a pivot in each of the $2$ coefficient columns, so the proposed vectors are linearly independent. The system is consistent, so the last vector is in their span. Their span therefore equals $U$, and $\\mathcal{B}$ is a basis.\n\nThe coefficients are $x_{1}=-2$, $x_{2}=-1$.\nThus\n$$\nx_1x_2=\\left(-2\\right)\\left(-1\\right)=2.\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714432 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44bc75de-eaf0-59b1-b9a5-5afcf7438c9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714415} {:answer/id #uuid "6724bfaa-4e73-53d0-b0c4-9bb1e433d912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714422} {:answer/id #uuid "a2586d0e-7349-55e0-a3a2-d5283e766fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714431} {:answer/id #uuid "e21cde68-e23b-54d1-bc88-0921c21b4e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714440} {:answer/id #uuid "eca45b38-6eb1-5e39-a370-a67c74978e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6724bfaa-4e73-53d0-b0c4-9bb1e433d912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714422} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b0723e9-70c3-51bb-bcdb-3c3511826928" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aa3d53b2-920d-5705-a338-d95eb30c2113" :question/problem "The vectors are given below.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nDetermine whether $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is a basis of $U=\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}$. If it is, find $x_1x_2$, where $\\mathbf{a}_3=x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2$. Otherwise, select the statement that it is not a basis." :question/worked-solution "A basis must be linearly independent and span $U$. The decomposition gives the system\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x_{1}-2x_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -x_{1}+2x_{2} &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nIts augmented matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{1}\\leftarrow \\left(-1\\right)R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow R_{2}+R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)R_{2}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{1}\\leftarrow R_{1}-2R_{2}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThe reduced matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThere is a pivot in each of the $2$ coefficient columns, so the proposed vectors are linearly independent. The system is consistent, so the last vector is in their span. Their span therefore equals $U$, and $\\mathcal{B}$ is a basis.\n\nThe coefficients are $x_{1}=3$, $x_{2}=-1$.\nThus\n$$\nx_1x_2=\\left(3\\right)\\left(-1\\right)=-3.\n$$\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a0fdbf-84f5-5f15-b654-7dfc8fcee7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714412} {:answer/id #uuid "5344fb3d-13a0-5e74-8005-892697826861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714417} {:answer/id #uuid "bf618178-d7bc-586e-afae-ba0e32da6cea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714437} {:answer/id #uuid "c39413a1-cd2c-5c4e-b1ac-b830b82d8725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714438} {:answer/id #uuid "f953e54c-ca4b-5bbd-a42e-e0f7b248de5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c39413a1-cd2c-5c4e-b1ac-b830b82d8725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714438} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c1e3597-df60-52d3-b42c-0ddc92ac8c85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bbb6f0c6-2fd7-5779-bf8c-e10a1e2f9114" :question/problem "The vectors are given below.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nDetermine whether $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is a basis of $U=\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}$. If it is, find $x_1x_2$, where $\\mathbf{a}_3=x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2$. Otherwise, select the statement that it is not a basis." :question/worked-solution "A basis must be linearly independent and span $U$. The decomposition gives the system\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x_{1}-2x_{2} &=8 \\\\ x_{1}-x_{2} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nIts augmented matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{1}\\leftarrow \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow R_{2}-R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThe reduced matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nOnly $1$ coefficient columns contain pivots. Thus the proposed vectors are linearly dependent. There is no contradictory row, so the last vector is in their span and they do span $U$. However, spanning alone does not make a basis. Therefore, $\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$; the conditional coefficient calculation does not apply."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00cf09a5-dd87-5767-bd6c-6f6814591358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714473} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9133b2-33ac-50bc-adfb-31326d34c3cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714478} {:answer/id #uuid "56b5a596-9bd8-51cc-9c16-947b66b45247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714483} {:answer/id #uuid "e78d9429-a67a-5131-a583-6ded3df067be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714498} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b2485b-870b-5fc5-b074-2e5ef04e9378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00cf09a5-dd87-5767-bd6c-6f6814591358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714473} :answer-field/id #uuid "c42d55e7-659a-52a9-a191-1655b0f125c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2db243a8-d883-59d4-a32b-4a172e8939d6" :question/problem "The vectors are given below.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nDetermine whether $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is a basis of $U=\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}$. If it is, find $x_1x_2$, where $\\mathbf{a}_3=x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2$. Otherwise, select the statement that it is not a basis.\n\nA basis must be **linearly independent** and *span* $U$. The augmented system for this decomposition has already been reduced:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n" :question/worked-solution "A basis must be linearly independent and span $U$. The decomposition gives the system\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x_{1}-x_{2} &=-3 \\\\ 6x_{1}+3x_{2} &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nIts augmented matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{1}\\leftarrow \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 6 & 3 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nApply $R_{2}\\leftarrow R_{2}-6R_{1}$:\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nThe reduced matrix is\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\nOnly $1$ coefficient columns contain pivots. Thus the proposed vectors are linearly dependent. There is no contradictory row, so the last vector is in their span and they do span $U$. However, spanning alone does not make a basis. Therefore, $\\mathcal{B}$ is not a basis of $U$; the conditional coefficient calculation does not apply."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fe817bc-5aae-5bb9-8b44-95601230727b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714480} {:answer/id #uuid "62ca9e7a-0959-52bf-af76-390c7ab06057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714485} {:answer/id #uuid "711842d6-2e71-57d7-9